{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "LAM",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember, O LORD, what is come upon us: consider, and behold our reproach.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Our inheritance is turned to strangers, our houses to aliens.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We are orphans and fatherless, our mothers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as widows.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We have drank our water for money; our wood is sold to us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Our necks ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " under persecution: we labor, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " have no rest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We have given the hand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Egyptians, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Assyrians, to be satisfied with bread.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Our fathers have sinned, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not; and we have borne their iniquities.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Servants have ruled over us: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none that doth deliver ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "us",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out of their hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We procured our bread with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the peril of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our lives, because of the sword of the wilderness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Our skin was black like an oven because of the terrible famine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They ravished the women in Zion, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the maids in the cities of Judah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Princes were hanged by their hand: the faces of elders were not honored.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They took the young men to grind, and the children fell under the wood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The elders have ceased from the gate, the young men from their music.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The joy of our heart hath ceased; our dance is turned into mourning.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The crown is fallen ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our head: woe to us, that we have sinned!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this our heart is faint; for these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our eyes are dim.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because of the mountain of Zion, which is desolate, the foxes walk upon it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou, O LORD, remainest for ever; thy throne from generation to generation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why dost thou forget us for ever, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " forsake us so long time?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Turn thou us to thee, O LORD, and we shall be turned; renew our days as of old.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LAM.5.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LAM.5.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But thou hast utterly rejected us; thou art very wroth against us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
